### Fail-closed and resource evidence

- Every pre-effect authentication failure leaves the fake client untouched, BudgetLedger at zero calls/reservations, the temp authorization ledger without a call reservation, and the temp audit trail empty.
- Definite pre-send failures release both reservations at zero. Any invocation that could have begun retains the full conservative uncertainty. Authoritative responses reconcile exact reported usage before any cap error is raised.
- Terminal provider records are immutable and content-free; they bind call/iteration/model/pricing/lifecycle/accounting facts and the post-reconciliation budget snapshot. No prompt, source, raw response, header, credential, or approval-reference value is recorded.
